# The podman producer: the `mica-podman` package -- the seven self-built
# container-engine binaries, the Quadlet generator symlink, and the container
# configuration PLAN-036 section 3 assigns to this package rather than to the
# common system overlay. Read by build-env/deb/producers.sh and
# build-env/deb/build.sh; the convention is documented in
# build-env/deb/README.md.
PACKAGES="mica-podman"

# This producer repacks upstream software, so its archive carries the upstream
# version in front of the pool's git stamp: mica-podman_5.8.6+git<commit>-1,
# not the workspace's 0.1.0. PODMAN_VERSION is the principal upstream; the
# component pins compiled in beside it (crun, conmon, netavark, aardvark-dns,
# catatonit) stay in the same versions.env and are asserted against the
# binaries by tests/install-closure-gate.sh -- a dpkg version string is not
# a list, so they do not ride in the version.
VERSION_FROM="versions.env:PODMAN_VERSION"

# NOT `all`. This payload is seven ELF binaries per architecture, so there is
# one archive per pool and dpkg-shlibdeps has to resolve each of them against
# its own architecture's libraries.
ARCHES="amd64 arm64"

# ZERO, AND THE ZERO IS THE DECLARATION. Two separate facts, both deliberate,
# and a future "helpful" enablement link is a privilege-escalation path rather
# than a convenience:
#
#   1. podman ships NO systemd service units at all. Upstream's units live in
#      contrib/ and are installed by `make install.systemd`, which
#      mica-podman does not run; rootfs/stages/31-feature-containers
#      asserts that no unit named podman* exists anywhere in the image. There is
#      no unit here for a multi-user.target.wants link to name.
#
#   2. The one unit in this payload, etc-containers-systemd.mount, is installed
#      and deliberately NOT enabled. rootfs/scripts/overlay-install.sh links
#      ten units into local-fs.target.wants and excludes this one, recording
#      why: statically enabled, "the bind comes up at every boot regardless of
#      container.enabled, Quadlet generates units from STATE, and they start --
#      so anything able to write /mnt/state/quadlet has a root-capable container
#      at the next reboot with no operator decision in the path. micad's
#      ContainerReconciler enables and starts it when the setting says true".
#      Its [Install] section stays, so that runtime enablement keeps working.
ENABLEMENT="mica-podman=0"

# The seven binaries are compiled from six pinned upstreams by
# build.sh, which is a four-toolchain cross build and not
# something a key here could describe.
PREPARE="prepare.sh"

# prepare.sh honours MOS_DEB_PREFLIGHT=1: asked that way it reports whether
# out-<arch> exists, holds all seven binaries and carries a stamp matching the
# current versions.env, and it builds NOTHING. Without this the answer arrives
# only when this producer's turn comes, and it arrives as three quarters of an
# hour of emulated compiling started from inside a packaging hook -- the most
# expensive late discovery in this repository, which is exactly what
# build-env/deb/preflight.sh exists to move to the front.
PREFLIGHT="1"

FROM_IMAGES="MOS_BUILD_DEB=LOCAL_MOS_BUILD_DEB"

# The container configuration and the Quadlet mount unit live in overlay/ of
# this repository: PLAN-036 section 3 gives them to mica-podman, and the split
# moved them here with the producer. The context is the overlay root so the
# paths this Dockerfile COPYs are the paths the files are installed to.
BUILD_CONTEXTS="overlay=overlay"
